  "source_id": "county-068",
  "text": "Elections | Orange County, NC\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account\n- Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nHow Do I...\nGovernment\nVisiting\nBusiness\nServices\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments A - F\nElections\nElections\nSkip to the bottom of the page\nThe Board of Elections provides Orange County with fair, efficient, convenient, and accurate elections within the guidelines of State and Federal Election Laws.\nIn addition to preparing for and conducting all elections within Orange County, the Board of Elections is responsible for processing and maintaining all Orange County voter registration records.\nNext Election\nGeneral Election: November 3, 2026\n2026 Election Schedule\n2026 Candidate list\nVoter Guide for the Nov. 3, 2026 General Election\n(PDF Tri-fold)\nVoting locations, maps, and sample ballots\nEarly voting information for the November 3, 2026, General Election\nPrintable PDF of the early voting plan\nPast Elections\nTo see results from past elections,\nvisit the N.C. State Board of Elections website\n. Select an election date, then search for Orange County.\nOur Services\nRegister to vote\nor update your voter registration.\nEarly voting:\nOrange County allows all eligible, registered voters to vote early in person. If you decide to vote on Election Day, you must vote at your assigned polling place.\nView the Early voting plan for the November 3, 2026, General Election.\nAbsentee voting by mail:\nOrange County allows all registered voters to vote by mail if they prefer.\nA photo ID is required for voting.\nGet a free photo ID for voting purposes if you do not have an acceptable ID by visiting our office Monday \u2013 Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. at 208 S. Cameron St., Hillsborough.\nFile to run for office\n.\nGet Assistance\nSearch for your\nvoter registration information\n.\nView\nsample ballots\n.\nView\nmaps of districts\n.\nView election day\npolling sites\n.\nView UNC-Chapel Hill\nresidence hall addresses\n.\nCancel\nyour voter registration.\nNotify of a deceased voter for\nregistration removal\n.\nVoter eligibility information for people serving\nfelony sentences\n.\nFind out where you vote\non Election Day.\nFind out if you are registered to vote\nby using the\nVoter Search Tool\n.\nGet help with\nabsentee voting\nby\nemailing\nor calling our office at 919-245-2353.\nLearn more about\ncampaign finance\n, required treasurer training, and rules about political signs.\nDirect questions about campaign finance to 919-245-2350 or to\nbcolson@orangecountync.gov\n.\nCampaign Disclosure Reports\nView\nfrequently asked questions\n.\nThe State Board of Elections is checking voter registrations through a\nVoter Registration Repair Project\nto fix missing North Carolina driver\u2019s license or ID numbers, or the last four digits of Social Security numbers.\nVisit our\nOutreach Resources\npage\nfor information on voter registration, absentee voting, photo ID for voting, and precinct information.\nRequest assistance with\nlanguage access\n.\nGet information on\npublic officials\nat different levels of government.\nCounty and Municipal Officials\nOrange County\nTown of Carrboro\nTown of Chapel Hill\nTown of Hillsborough\nSchool Boards\nOrange County Board of Education\nChapel Hill-Carrboro Board of Education\nState, Federal and Judicial Officials\nState Officials\nFederal Officials\nJudicial Officials\nQualifications\nfor office\nGet Involved\nThe Orange County Board of Elections\nis comprised of five dedicated members who are entrusted with administering fair, secure, and accessible elections for all county residents.\nWant to serve democracy by\nworking on Election Day\n? Complete an\ninterest form\n.\nView\nelection-related links\nfor Orange County\n, North Carolina and the broader area.\nView past results from\nprior elections\n.\nOrganize a\nvoter registration drive\n.\nContact Us\nWebsite:\nwww.orangecountync.gov/Elections\nPhone:\n919-245-2350\nFax:\n919-644-3318\nEmail:\nvote@orangecountync.gov\nPhysical Address:\n208 S. Cameron St., Hillsborough, NC 27278\nMailing Address:\nP.O. Box 220, Hillsborough, NC 27278\nEmail Your Absentee Voting Inquiry\n.\nEmail Your Campaign Finance Inquiry\nAbout the Office\nOrange County Board of Elections Director, Rachel Raper: 919-245-2351,\nrraper@orangecountync.gov\nView the full\nstaff directory\nCurrent legal notices\nFAQs\nI am registered unaffiliated, may I vote in a Primary Election?\nWhen is the deadline to register to vote in an election?\nWhen are the polls open?\nView All FAQs\n/FAQ.aspx\nHours and Additional Information\nThe Orange County Board of Elections offices are open\nMonday \u2013 Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m.\nThey are closed on\ncertain holidays\nthroughout the year.\nIf you need information in another format or language or need an accommodation, please contact us at the\nLanguage Access Services\npage\n.\nPhoto ID- REQUIRED for Voting\nBoard of Elections Members & Meetings\nFiling for Office\nVoter Registration Repair Project\nEarly Voting\nEarly Voting Wait Time Tracker\nVoter Registration\nAbsentee Voting By Mail\nSample Ballots, Maps, & Voting Location Info\nOutreach Resources\nWork in Elections\nPublic Officials\nCounty & Municipal Officials\nOrange County\nTown of Carrboro\nTown of Chapel Hill\nTown of Hillsborough\nCity of Mebane\nSchool Boards\nOrange County Board of Education\nChapel Hill Carrboro Board of Education\nState, Federal & Judicial Officials\nFederal Officials\nJudicial Officials\nState Officials\nQualifications for Office\nCampaign Finance Reports & Sign Info\nCampaign Disclosure Reports\nLegal Notices\nElection Related Links\nPast Results\nLimited English Proficiency Services\nBoard of Commissioners\nEmployment\nPay Your Taxes\nPermit Portal\nAdopt a Pet\nRegister of Deeds\nContact Us\n300 West Tryon Street\nP.O. Box 8181\nHillsborough, NC 27278\nPhone:\n919-732-8181\nContact the Webmaster\nQuick Links\nLegal Notices\nRequest Public Records\nIntranet (employees only)\nPublic Participation Policy\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHome\nSite Map\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nPrivacy Policy\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
